        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: complete C1 control-character (0x80-0x9f) coverage across terminal/log sinks",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nConsolidates C1 control-character (U+0080–U+009F) detection, stripping, escaping, replacement, or rejection across terminal, command, diagnostic, attachment-name, and logging boundaries.\n\nThis PR supersedes 8+ single-sink C1 hardening proposals (#103226, #103379, #103380, #103381, #103382, and others) into one canonical fix.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nValidates actual production `sanitizeForConsole` function with C1 characters:\n\n```\n=== sanitizeForConsole — C1 control-character stripping ===\n\n  ✓ C1 U+0080 (PAD) stripped — \"\\^@\" removed\n  ✓ C1 U+009F (APC) stripped — \"\\^_\" removed\n  ✓ C1 U+0090 (DCS) stripped — \"\\^P\" removed\n  ✓ multiple C1 chars stripped — \"\\^@\\^_\\^P\" all removed\n  ✓ C0 DEL (0x7F) stripped (existing coverage)\n  ✓ C0 NUL (0x00) stripped (existing coverage)\n  ✓ normal ASCII unchanged — \"Hello, world!\" preserved\n  ✓ Unicode/emoji preserved — emoji characters pass through\n\n✅ 8 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `pnpm build:ci-artifacts` → exit 0 ✓\n- Focused regression tests cover C1 detection across multiple sink boundaries\n- 25 files changed across terminal, hooks, doctor, sandbox, subagent, and config paths\n\n/cc @openclaw/clawsweeper",
